  clock: 2  # 97df
  nonce: 97df  # 97df
  message: "CORRECTION: THE HOST BOUNDARY HAS A THIRD OUTCOME, AND MY AUDIT MISSED IT.\n\nThis row's description asserts the WI-didil contract as background -- every\nregistered analyzer resolves to exactly one of an analysis_runs entry or a\nlimits.skipped_passes entry -- and treats the defect as WHICH of the two a pass\nlands in. There is a third outcome: NEITHER.\n\nMEASURED 2026-09-17 with HYPERGUMBO_RUST_ANALYZER=1 on aardvark-dns:\n\n    analysis_runs 74 + skipped_passes 84 = 158\n    rust_analyzer in neither, and it is the ONLY one of 118 registered\n    analyzers for which that is true.\n\nIt happens on the SUCCESS path: the analyzer returns\nAnalysisResult(symbols=..., edges=...) with no run=, and\ncollect_analyzer_result's run-is-None branch records a skip only when\nproduced_nothing is true. A producer that emitted output without a run is\ndrained and silently dropped from the accounting -- deliberately, per that\nbranch's own comment. 669 nodes and 637 edges entered the artifact from a pass\nthat appears nowhere in the pass catalog.\n\nWHY MY AUDIT DID NOT SEE IT. My survey ran with the backend at its default\n(off), so rust_analyzer reported backend_disabled into skipped_passes and the\naccounting looked complete. The third outcome is only reachable with an opt-in\nflag no CI run or bakeoff sets. A one-repo, default-configuration measurement\ncould not have found it, and I did not say so at the time -- the audit's \"what\nthis did NOT establish\" section should have named configuration coverage\nalongside corpus coverage.\n\nWHAT IT CHANGES FOR THIS ROW. Nothing about the 130-of-162 finding, which\nstands. But option (3) in the proposed shape -- \"make the host a function of\nthe fact\" -- must now account for three outcomes, not two, and the union helper\nin option (2) must be built over the pass catalog rather than over\nanalysis_runs + skipped_passes, or it will silently omit any pass in neither\nbucket. That is a real design constraint on the helper, not a caveat.\n\nRoot cause of the third outcome is filed separately as WI-didag; it is a bug\nwith a one-threading fix and does not need the owner decision this row raises."  # 97df
